1. DEFINITIONS AND SCOPE

1.1 Software means the original PHP, Blade, CSS, JavaScript, configuration,
    designs, assets and accompanying materials distributed as FLEX Theme,
    including modified copies and original package code incorporated into
    another work. Independently authored application code and user data are
    not owned by the Licensor merely because they integrate with the Software.
    Filament, Laravel, FLEX Fields, FLEX Forms, icons and other third-party
    packages are separate products governed by their respective terms.

1.2 You / Licensee means the one natural person or one legal entity identified
    in the accepted order. A company is distinct from its employees, owners,
    clients, parent, subsidiaries, affiliates and other companies. Common
    ownership, a shared developer, invoice or server does not combine licensees.
    An authorized purchaser may accept this License on that entity's behalf.

1.3 Order means a completed purchase through the Licensor's official checkout
    or an expressly accepted written agreement identifying the Licensee, plan,
    applicable License version and paid scope. The official Lemon Squeezy order
    confirmation and associated license key are sufficient purchase evidence;
    a separate registration, negotiated agreement or manual approval is not
    required for a standard purchase. A license key is a credential and evidence
    of the Order, not a bearer instrument transferable to whoever possesses it.

1.4 Production Domain means one normalized hostname at which the licensed
    application is made available for real operations, including staff-only,
    customer, tenant, free-tier or paid-pilot operations. Case, scheme, port,
    path, query string, trailing dot and an optional leading www. do not create
    separate domains. Other hostnames and subdomains count separately. Thus
    example.com and www.example.com are one domain; admin.example.com,
    app.example.com and example.org are three. Multiple native Filament panels
    and paths within one licensed application at the same hostname do not use
    extra domain slots. Hosting unrelated applications behind one hostname,
    proxy or gateway does not make them one licensed application.

1.5 Production includes actual business operations regardless of the hostname,
    privacy, access restrictions, revenue, user count or an environment's name.
    A live installation does not become development by naming it staging,
    localhost, demo, preview or test, or by hiding it behind authentication.

1.6 Authorized Personnel means employees and contractors, including an agency
    or hosting/build provider, accessing the Software solely to work on the
    Licensee's permitted applications. They must protect copies and credentials
    against unauthorized reuse and disclosure and receive no independent
    license for themselves, their other clients or unrelated applications.
    The Licensee is responsible for the access it authorizes.

1.7 Browser Assets means the HTML, CSS, JavaScript, fonts and other resources
    ordinarily delivered to browsers to operate a licensed application. Runtime
    Access means using that application's interface without receiving reusable
    package source, server files, deployment artifacts or independent rights
    to install, copy, operate or distribute the Software.

1.8 Official Channels means the Licensor's protected package service and other
    expressly authorized delivery channels. The public repository
    github.com/janczakb/filament-flex-theme contains documentation and legal
    materials; the implementation is distributed from the private package
    repository through the protected service. Another customer's vendor folder,
    shared key, leaked archive, mirror or purchased third-party copy is not an
    Official Channel and does not establish a license.

