3. PLANS — IDENTICAL FEATURES, DIFFERENT DOMAIN ALLOWANCES

3.1 SINGLE grants one Licensee use in one identified application at one
    Production Domain at a time. Additional application identities or production
    hostnames require additional Single licenses or an Unlimited license.
    A Single license is not an agency-wide or client-pool license.

3.2 UNLIMITED grants one Licensee use in any number of applications and at any
    number of Production Domains for that Licensee's own operations and hosted
    services. It does not license separate companies or independently owned
    client applications, even when the same agency builds or maintains them.
    Authorized Personnel may assist the Licensee under Section 1.6. Unlimited
    does not mean unlimited redistribution, sublicensing, OEM or resale rights.

3.3 Both plans include the same Software features. Neither imposes a separate
    developer-seat, end-user, server, CPU or revenue limit within its licensed
    scope. Multiple servers, replicas and regions for a permitted deployment do
    not consume additional domain slots. Production tenant/custom hostnames
    follow the same domain rule; a tenant is not an independent package licensee.

3.4 The Licensee may provide paid or unpaid Runtime Access to its own licensed
    hosted application. Its users receive no right to download the package,
    reuse its code, independently operate the application or sublicense it.
    White-label application branding is allowed; relabeling or reselling FLEX
    Theme itself, and transferring independent reseller/OEM rights, are not.

3.5 A genuine domain migration may replace the registered hostname for the
    same application. Remove or deactivate the old production use before the
    new one becomes independently operational; a short technical cutover is
    allowed solely to migrate that application. Deactivation does not authorize
    rotating a Single key among concurrently operating sites or unrelated apps.
    The portal's activation rules remain applicable; if an expired key cannot
    be reassigned automatically, contact the Licensor for a same-application
    migration. There is no promise of perpetual activation infrastructure.

