    does not convert lawful continued use into an annual rental obligation.

5.2 A standard purchase includes one year of access to updates actually
    published for this package during its update period, including major
    versions if published within that period. The official order and provider
    expiry timestamp identify the start and end of that period. Separate
    products or add-ons are excluded. No minimum number or frequency of updates,
    new features, fixes, framework upgrades or future releases is promised.

5.3 After expiry, new releases published after the cutoff require renewed
    update entitlement or a new purchase. Versions released on or before the
    cutoff remain eligible for the paid usage grant and for re-download while
    the protected distribution service operates, subject to legitimate access
    checks. Do not infer an automatic extension of an old key from purchasing
    a different key. A renewal's duration and effect must be disclosed in its
    accepted order; ordinary one-time purchases do not automatically recur.

5.4 Keep your own permitted copies and deployment backups. Update entitlement
    is not an indefinite cloud-storage, archive-hosting, activation or support
    subscription. You remain responsible for retaining the versions you need.
    There is no promise to preserve every dependency, remote font, API, external
    service or development environment indefinitely.

5.5 PRODUCT LIFECYCLE. The Licensor may evolve, replace, discontinue or stop
    maintaining the Software and may retire download, activation, update and
    other hosted services. No obligation to operate the business, maintain
    servers, publish updates or support old framework versions indefinitely is
    created by a perpetual usage license. Such retirement does not revoke your
    paid rights to eligible versions or prevent use of lawfully retained copies.

5.6 For an orderly permanent retirement, the Licensor will give reasonable
    advance notice where practicable, normally aiming for at least 30 days,
    and a reasonable opportunity to obtain and retain available eligible
    versions. Urgent legal, security or circumstances beyond reasonable control
    may require shorter notice or immediate suspension. No notice can guarantee
